	IMAO, Fire Brand is underrated, and Frost Brand is overrated,
probably because the artifact spoiler ranks them primarily by their
performance against demon lords, which are all fire resistant.

	I find that the demon lords are, for the most part, pushovers by
the time I get to them. I'm not worried about how my weapon's going to
perform against one horribly outclassed demon lord. I'm more concerned
about performance against the monsters that can surround me and swamp
me, especially in the endgame. And most undead and all the Angels are
cold resistant, but few of them are fire resistant.

	That means that in the Valley, in the Sanctum, on the Astral,
Fire Brand is far superior to Frost Brand. On the Plane of Fire, Frost
Brand is obviously superior, but if you're fire resistant (and what are
you doing there if you're not?), most of the denizens are harmless
anyway. I don't even bother fighting them unless they won't get out of
my way... I just walk past, ignoring them completely.

	In any case, Fire Brand is a top-tier artifact weapon, below
Grayswandir and possibly Mjollnir, but right up there with Frosty.

